. Tedford, T. Potzel, K. Pfeffer, and K.D. Fischer. <year>2001</year>. Lsc is required for marginal zone B cells, regulation of lymphocyte motility and immune responses. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>855</fpage>&#x02013;862.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11526402</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Won, W.J., and J.F. Kearney. <year>2002</year>. CD9 is a unique marker for marginal zone B cells, B1 cells, and plasma cells in mice. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>168</volume>:<fpage>5605</fpage>&#x02013;5611.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12023357</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Crowley, M.T., C.R. Reilly, and D. Lo. <year>1999</year>. Influence of lymphocytes on the presence and organization of dendritic cell subsets in the spleen. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>163</volume>:<fpage>4894</fpage>&#x02013;4900.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10528191</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Tumanov, A., D. Kuprash, M. Lagarkova, S. Grivennikov, K. Abe, A. Shakhov, L. Drutskaya, C. Stewart, A. Chervonsky, and S. Nedospasov. <year>2002</year>. Distinct role of surface lymphotoxin expressed by B cells in the organization of secondary lymphoid tissues. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>239</fpage>&#x02013;250.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12354378</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Amano, M., N. Baumgarth, M.D. Dick, L. Brossay, M. Kronenberg, L.A. Herzenberg, and S. Strober. <year>1998</year>. CD1 expression defines subsets of follicular and marginal zone B cells in the spleen: beta 2-microglobulin-dependent and independent forms. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>161</volume>:<fpage>1710</fpage>&#x02013;1717.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9712035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><label>25</label><citatio